id="chatgpt">ChatGPT (Developer mode) Connect it once — ChatGPT is key-less, so there is no config file to edit and no key to store: Enable Developer mode : chatgpt.com → Settings → Security and login → Developer mode (Plus / Pro / Business / Enterprise / Education). Open chatgpt.com/plugins → the + button → create a Developer-mode app. MCP server URL: https://api.premiselabs.co/mcp — no API key. Use the URL exactly as written, with no trailing slash. Choose OAuth ; ChatGPT discovers Tortoise's authorization server automatically. Click Scan Tools , sign in to Tortoise when prompted, and click Authorize . When Tortoise asks which organization to connect, choose the one you want this graph in. Start a new chat at chatgpt.com (if the Tortoise tools don't appear, re-open chatgpt.com/plugins and re-check the Scan Tools result). Open app.premiselabs.co/skills/tortoise-onboarding/SKILL.md in a browser, copy the whole document, and paste it into that chat — ChatGPT has no local skills, so this document is what onboards it (if the agent can open the link itself, that works too). Ask it to set up Tortoise: it follows those instructions to verify the connection and file your first memory — th

